Feature: Trending Movies response record migration

Overview
- Refactor `BookController#getTrendingMovies` (`mbooks-quarkus`) to stop building the response body
  by hand with `org.json.JSONObject`/`JSONArray`, and instead serialize dedicated top-level `record`
  response models via a dedicated mapper class.
- Contract ID: CID-MBOOKS-TRENDING (see `.ai/retrieval/references/CONTRACTS_INDEX.md`).
- This is an internal implementation refactor only. The public HTTP contract
  (`GET /rest/book/trending-movies`, query params, status codes, JSON field names/types) MUST NOT
  change for existing consumers (`@frontend-dev`, `@ios-dev`).

Baseline (as-found)
- Endpoint: `mbooks-quarkus/src/main/java/com/jeet/rest/BookController.java` (`getTrendingMovies`,
  path `/book/trending-movies`, class-level base path resolves it under `/rest`).
- Validation (`days >= 1`, `limit` in `1..50`) and error responses (`400`/`500`) are built manually
  as `JSONObject` and returned via `Response`.
- Success body is assembled manually: `JSONArray` of `JSONObject` items, wrapped in a
  `JSONObject` under key `trendingMovies`.
- Data source: `BookingHandlerImpl#getTrendingMovies(int days, int limit)` →
  `DAO#getTrendingMovies(int days, int limit)`, returning `List<com.jeet.api.TrendingMovieRow>`.
- `TrendingMovieRow` (`com.jeet.api.TrendingMovieRow`) already exists as a plain class with:
  `movieId` (int), `name` (String), `thumbnail_picture` (String, defaults to `""`),
  `large_picture` (String, defaults to `""`), `bookedTickets` (long),
  `lastBookingTime` (String, ISO-8601 or `null`).
- `pom.xml` already includes `quarkus-resteasy-jackson`, so Jackson (with Java `record` support)
  is available for automatic JSON serialization without adding a new dependency.

Functional requirements

REQ-TMR-1 Response model types
- Introduce two new top-level `record` types, not nested inside the mapper class:
  - `com.jeet.rest.responserecord.TrendingMoviesResponse(List<TrendingMovieItem> trendingMovies)`
  - `com.jeet.rest.responserecord.TrendingMovieItem(int movieId, String name, String thumbnail_picture,
    String large_picture, long bookedTickets, String lastBookingTime)`
- `lastBookingTime` MUST remain `String` (not `Instant`), matching `TrendingMovieRow`'s existing
  type and the documented ISO-8601-or-null contract in the README/CID. Introducing an `Instant`
  field would silently change the serialized JSON shape and is out of scope here.

REQ-TMR-2 Mapper
- Add `com.jeet.rest.TrendingMoviesMapper` (or `com.jeet.mapper.TrendingMoviesMapper`), an
  `@ApplicationScoped` CDI bean with a single responsibility: convert
  `List<TrendingMovieRow>` → `TrendingMoviesResponse`.
- Mapper MUST preserve current null-safety behavior:
  - `thumbnail_picture`/`large_picture`: already normalized to `""` inside `TrendingMovieRow`;
    mapper must not re-introduce `null`.
  - `lastBookingTime`: pass through as-is (`null` stays `null`; current behavior serializes this
    as JSON `null` via `JSONObject.NULL` — Jackson serializes a `null` record component the same
    way by default, so no extra handling is required).

REQ-TMR-3 Controller behavior preserved
- The controller method signature, `@GET`/`@Path("/book/trending-movies")`/`@Produces` annotations,
  and query param validation (`days < 1` → `400`; `limit` outside `1..50` → `400`) MUST be
  unchanged.
- The controller MUST keep returning `jakarta.ws.rs.core.Response` (not the bare record type) so
  that the existing `400`/`500` error-response construction and status codes are untouched.
- On the success path, replace the manual `JSONArray`/`JSONObject` construction with:
  `Response.ok(trendingMoviesMapper.toResponse(rows)).type(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON).build()`,
  relying on Jackson to serialize the `TrendingMoviesResponse` record.
- The existing structured log line (`days`, `limit`, `resultSize`) MUST be preserved.

REQ-TMR-4 Backward-compatible JSON shape
- Serialized JSON for the success path MUST be field-for-field identical to today's output:
  root key `trendingMovies`, item keys `movieId`, `name`, `thumbnail_picture`, `large_picture`,
  `bookedTickets`, `lastBookingTime` (string or `null`), same value types.
- Empty result window MUST still produce `{"trendingMovies": []}`.

REQ-TMR-5 Error paths unaffected
- `400` (`INVALID_PARAM`) and `500` (`INTERNAL_ERROR`) JSON error payloads and status codes are
  unchanged; no migration to record-backed error bodies in this feature (kept out of scope to
  minimize blast radius).

Non-functional requirements

REQ-TMR-NF-1 No new runtime dependency
- Use the Jackson provider already pulled in by `quarkus-resteasy-jackson`. Do not add JSON-B or
  another serialization library.

REQ-TMR-NF-2 Testability
- `TrendingMoviesMapper` must be unit-testable in isolation (plain input `List<TrendingMovieRow>`,
  plain output `TrendingMoviesResponse`), independent of JAX-RS/CDI request context.

Acceptance criteria
- [ ] `TrendingMoviesResponse` and `TrendingMovieItem` exist as separate top-level records in
      `com.jeet.api`.
- [ ] `TrendingMoviesMapper` exists as a separate class with no response record nested inside it.
- [ ] `BookController#getTrendingMovies` delegates response construction to
      `TrendingMoviesMapper` and no longer builds `JSONArray`/`JSONObject` for the success body.
- [ ] Existing validation and error-response behavior (`400`/`500`) is unchanged.
- [ ] `GET /rest/book/trending-movies` produces byte-for-byte equivalent JSON field names/types
      versus current behavior for a non-empty and an empty result set.
- [ ] Module compiles (`mvn -DskipTests compile`) and existing tests (if any cover this endpoint)
      still pass.
- [ ] README section for the trending-movies endpoint requires no contract changes (verify, do
      not rewrite unless drift is found).
